{"config": "A-dense-gptoss20b", "qid": "A34", "type": "answerable", "version_sensitive": true, "answer": "Under the KYC Master Direction, the periodic update of KYC must be performed at least once every two years for high‑risk customers, once every eight years for medium‑risk customers, and once every ten years for low‑risk customers (from the date of opening of the account or last KYC update).  However, for an individual customer who is low‑risk, the RBI allows KYC to be updated within one year of the due date or up to 30 June 2026, whichever is later. Note: \"Master Direction - Know Your Customer (KYC) Direction, 2016\" (issued 2016-02-25) has been withdrawn or superseded and replaced by entity-wise KYC Directions, 2025. The rule currently in force may differ.", "citations": ["D12_A_0041"], "refused": false, "refusal_reason": "", "invalid_citations": [], "superseded_cited": ["D12_A_0041"], "injection_detected": false, "cost_usd": 0.00027179999999999994, "gen_latency_s": 0.7911220000096364, "rate_limit_wait_s": 0.0, "usage": {"input_tokens": 3160, "output_tokens": 212, "cache_read_input_tokens": 768, "billed_cost_usd": 0.0002718, "provider": "Groq", "via": "openrouter"}, "retrieved": ["D12_A_0041", "D12_A_0046", "D12_A_0045", "D12_A_0042", "D12_A_0047"], "retrieval_latency_s": 0.04174209998745937, "total_latency_s": 0.8329796000034548, "hit@5": 1, "rr@10": 1.0, "first_hit_rank": 1, "gold_cited": true}
